ABI 12 (mt_engine_abi_version() returns 12; one struct added, none
changed) adds it to mtproto_engine.h:
  uint64_t mt_route_check_start(MTEngine *engine, const MTRouteCheck *check);
  void mt_route_check_cancel(MTEngine *engine, uint64_t check);
with MTRouteCheck (address, obfuscation_dc_id, framing, proxy,
proxy_addresses and proxy_address_count, time_difference,
tls_hello_time_offset, timeout) and MTEventKindRouteChecked (39): code
1 when answered, else 0, value1 the round trip in seconds, text the
reason, integer1 the attempts. The setup, the strings it points to and
the offset are copied during the call; the setup and the offset are
read unaligned, as 32-bit MSVC can place a local double, or a struct
holding one, at an address Rust's f64 does not allow. Proxy addresses
that are not IP literals, and repeats, are skipped, as
mt_session_set_proxy_addresses skips them. 0 comes back, and nothing
starts, for a null engine or setup and for a WEB proxy. The ABI version
checks, the C layout test (MTRouteCheck's size and its fields'
offsets) and docs/swift-integration.md follow. Tests:
mtproto-ffi ffi_abi12::the_header_declares_abi_12,
